	"source": "Thresholds come from each state's salvage-title or total-loss statute or regulation, read by our editorial team in October 2026; each state lists its citation. Percentage states total a car when repair cost reaches the stated share of its actual cash value. Total Loss Formula states total it when repair cost plus salvage value reaches its value. Where state law sets no number, the insurer decides when repairs are uneconomical, and most insurers apply the Total Loss Formula. Verify with your state department of insurance before relying on this.",
